            <ArticleTitle>[A man with 2 painful feet].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D168</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 25-year-old man landed a jump with both feet against a vertical rock. He experienced a sharp pain in both ankles and was unable to walk without support. Active plantar flexion could not be performed and the Thompson test was abnormal. The diagnosis bilateral Achilles tendon rupture was made.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
